From: =?UTF-8?q?Trung=20L=C3=AA?= <8@tle.id.au>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:12:16 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add a Linux ppc64le build configuration

Add a POWER8-baseline clang toolchain, vcpkg triplet and
linux-ppc64le-clang{,-rwdi,-rel} presets. The engine's SSE code builds
against clang's PowerPC x86-intrinsic compatibility headers, so the
project defines NO_WARN_X86_INTRINSICS on ppc64le. It stays out of the
toolchain because vcpkg ports such as openal-soft would otherwise detect
SSE and use SSE2 calls the headers don't provide.

Report "ppc64le" in the version string instead of falling through to
"x86", and read the timebase register for terrain profiling timestamps
instead of returning 0.

Document the preset and VCPKG_FORCE_SYSTEM_BINARIES in the README, and
extracting the GOG offline installer with innoextract in the Linux
build guide.
---
 CMakeLists.txt                                |  8 +++++
 README.md                                     |  5 ++--
 cmake/presets/linux.json                      | 30 +++++++++++++++++++
 cmake/toolchains/linux-ppc64le-clang.cmake    | 11 +++++++
 .../vcpkg-triplets/ppc64le-linux-clang.cmake  |  9 ++++++
 docs/build/linux.md                           | 20 ++++++++++++-
 engine/Poseidon/UI/OptionsUIApp.cpp           |  2 ++
 .../Poseidon/World/Terrain/TerrainProfile.hpp |  2 ++
 8 files changed, 84 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 cmake/toolchains/linux-ppc64le-clang.cmake
 create mode 100644 cmake/vcpkg-triplets/ppc64le-linux-clang.cmake

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 9537cbd..179340a 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -80,6 +80,14 @@ if(UNIX AND NOT APPLE)
     endif()
 endif()
 
+# The engine's SSE code builds on POWER through clang's PowerPC <xmmintrin.h>/
+# <emmintrin.h> compatibility headers, which refuse to compile without this.
+# Kept out of the toolchain so vcpkg ports don't detect SSE and pick x86 paths
+# the headers only partly cover.
+if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR MATCHES "^(ppc64le|powerpc64le)$")
+    add_compile_definitions(NO_WARN_X86_INTRINSICS)
+endif()
+
 # Make __FILE__ repo-root-relative so log/assert lines (Fail(), DoAssert(), LOG_*)
 # read "engine/Poseidon/...:NN" instead of an absolute build-machine path. Affects only
 # the __FILE__ macro string, not debug info.
